9. TYPES OF FUNCTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------

Functions can be categorized based on:

A. Arguments
B. Return value


Type 1:
    No arguments, no return value

Example:

void display(void)
{
    printf("Hello\n");
}


Type 2:
    Arguments, no return value

Example:

void displayNumber(int n)
{
    printf("%d\n", n);
}


Type 3:
    No arguments, return value

Example:

int getNumber(void)
{
    return 100;
}


Type 4:
    Arguments and return value

Example:

int add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

This fourth type is extremely common.


