33. FUNCTION POINTERS
------------------------------------------------------------

A function pointer stores the address of a function.

Example:

int add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int (*operation)(int, int);

operation = add;

int result = operation(10, 20);

printf("%d", result);

Output:

