36. qsort() AND FUNCTION POINTERS
------------------------------------------------------------

The C standard library's qsort() uses a comparison function.

Example:

#include <stdlib.h>

int compare(const void *a, const void *b)
{
    int x = *(const int *)a;
    int y = *(const int *)b;

    return (x > y) - (x < y);
}

int arr[] = {40, 10, 30, 20};

qsort(arr, 4, sizeof(arr[0]), compare);

This is an important real-world example of callbacks.


