86. GATE-LEVEL FUNCTION POINTER CONCEPT
------------------------------------------------------------

Given:

int add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int (*fp)(int, int) = add;

Then:

fp(2, 3)

is equivalent in effect to:

add(2, 3)

and produces:

5


